WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.900
Hollywood has a reputation for housing secrets,
but sometimes with major casting announcements,

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:09.250
the audience reaction winds up being something
like, "yawn, we already knew that" followed

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:12.040
by maybe a polite golf clap.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.340
"Golf clap?"

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.640
"Golf clap."

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.949
(golf clap)

00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:22.820
This is because, thanks to leaks and common
sense, the public already scooped the big

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.859
news long before the studio made it official.

00:00:24.859 --> 00:00:29.279
Here are a few of the worst-kept casting secrets
in Hollywood.

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:31.130
Brie Larson as Captain Marvel

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.411
There were a bunch of names in play as to
who'd become Captain Marvel in the Marvel

00:00:34.411 --> 00:00:39.530
Cinematic Universe, but once Brie Larson scored
her Best Actress Oscar for Room, she seemed

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:40.710
like the obvious choice.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:47.230
"Because I love the way that she, like, commands
herself and owns her, like, womanness."

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:50.690
She has the versatility, the critical cachet,
and she looks the part.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:54.879
So when rumors began that she was being considered
for the role, she seemed like a shoo-in.

00:00:54.879 --> 00:00:58.969
The studio's announcement at Comic-Con that
she'd been cast simply confirmed what fans

00:00:58.969 --> 00:01:01.150
had already suspected.

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:03.149
Alden Ehrenreich as Han Solo

00:01:03.149 --> 00:01:07.460
After Disney and Lucasfilm announced a Han
Solo standalone prequel to Star Wars, the

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.210
big question was who would play Young Han.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.170
Over 3,000 actors came out for the part, but
the Hail, Caesar!

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:17.220
star was considered the front-runner for weeks
before the studio revealed that they'd landed

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.580
Alden Ehrenreich.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:24.610
"This is the best kept secret in Hollywood.

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:30.259
The identity of this person is Alden Ehrenreich."

00:01:30.259 --> 00:01:33.560
The only thing that's been surprising about
this news, really, is that he's nabbed not

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.909
just one feature film, but a potential trilogy.

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:37.759
Hey, you know what Han would say.

00:01:37.759 --> 00:01:38.799
"I got him!"

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:40.909
"Great kid, now don't get cocky."

00:01:40.909 --> 00:01:43.470
Benedict Cumberbatch as Dr. Strange

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:47.560
Sherlock as the Sorcerer Supreme was considered
a winning combination ever since Benedict

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:50.940
Cumberbatch was first rumored to be attached
to the Marvel Phase 3 pic.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:54.200
Not only is he a fan favorite, he's also a
dead ringer for the character.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.460
So, when Marvel finally confirmed him as their
choice for the adaptation, it made perfect

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:00.159
sense.

00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:04.810
"This doesn't make any sense."

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:07.479
Adam Driver in Star Wars: The Force Awakens

00:02:07.479 --> 00:02:11.870
When Girls star Adam Driver was first rumored
to be attached to Star Wars: The Force Awakens,

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:14.180
many expected him to play the bad guy.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:18.480
After several red herring efforts to distract
from the possibility, LucasFilm finally confirmed

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.130
his casting, and he was indeed playing the
film's heavy, Kylo Ren.

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:26.780
In addition, as many also suspected, Ren is
the wayward son of Han Solo.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:29.780
Seems like the force was strong with the rumor
mill this time.

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:35.180
(heavy breathing for Anakin Skywalker's lightsaber)

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:38.650
Matthew McConaughey in The Dark Tower

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:42.540
The Oscar-winner was rumored to be circling
Stephen King's apocalyptic western for months

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:46.959
before King himself confirmed that Matthew
McConaughey and Idris Elba would star as Randall

00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:49.620
Flagg and gunslinger Roland Deschain respectively.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:54.160
The only real surprise for King fans is how
non-mythical the character is in the long-anticipated

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.129
movie version, as opposed to the mirage-like
creature he was in the books.

00:02:58.129 --> 00:03:01.630
Even so, the official announcement of McConaughey's
role was news to almost no one.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:02.849
"To that I say amen.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:06.610
To that I say alright, alright, alright."

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:08.849
Kurt Russell in Guardians of the Galaxy 2

00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:13.170
Fans of Marvel's Guardians of the Galaxy got
to watch in real-time as Kurt Russell was

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.569
cast in the sequel as Star-Lord's father.

00:03:15.569 --> 00:03:17.280
"You're half-Terran.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.100
Your mother was of Earth.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.100
Your father…

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:25.220
Well, he's something very ancient we've never
seen here before."

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:28.909
Once he was rumored to be eyeing the follow-up
film, reporters caught up to him only to learn

00:03:28.909 --> 00:03:31.290
that, at that time, he hadn't even seen the
first movie!

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:35.440
Still, Marvel eventually confirmed Russell
will indeed star in the film after all … as

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.180
a sentient planet that somehow fathered a
regular-sized human.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:41.220
Hey, if we can love a talking tree…

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:45.430
(I Want You Back by The Jackson 5 playing)

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:46.840
Thanks for watching!

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:49.760
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:54.249
And leave us a comment to let us know what
you think of these not-so-secret casting choices…

